:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396250}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4a35af51-a0e2-50d0-bbd3-1c0dc3bc52aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-183328" :question/problem "Describe the set $S={…,3,6,12,24,48,...}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n*Hint: Take ${a}_{1}=6$ in the sequence that generates the elements of $S.$*\n\n$$\nS={ {{field-1}}\\,:\\,n\\in {{field-2}} }\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n…,\\,3,\\,6,\\,12,\\,24,\\,48,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =2 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{12} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  ${a}_{1}=6,$ the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in Z$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =6\\cdot {2}^{n-1} \\\\  & =6\\cdot {2}^{n}\\cdot {2}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{2}\\cdot {2}^{n} \\\\  & =3\\cdot {2}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={3\\cdot {2}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in Z}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396254 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198465 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f49ef1c2-06de-597c-bf4d-6d613989987e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Set Using a Conditional Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b665804-beaa-5388-ac25-9397d16709cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396256} {:answer/id #uuid "cc29d216-b4b5-5d05-aee8-fa1d64f964da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396257} {:answer/id #uuid "80b0d143-f228-52ab-ad57-54619241a5e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb