key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287442}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "250dc34e-ac8d-50ac-8f72-1123fa8a7b34" :question/math-academy-id "q-183751" :question/problem "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set ${-3,-\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{5}}$ given below.\n\n${-3,-\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{5}}={x\\in R\\,:\\,3{x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-1}}\n${x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$x\\,-$\n{{field-3}}\n$=0}$" :question/worked-solution "The given set contains the roots $x\\in R$ of some cubic polynomial $p(x).$\n\nSince the cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-3,$ ${x}_{2}=-\\sqrt{5},$ and ${x}_{3}=\\sqrt{5},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =(3)(x-(-3))(x-(-\\sqrt{5}))(x-\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =3(x+3)(x+\\sqrt{5})(x-\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =3(x+3)({x}^{2}-\\sqrt{5}x+\\sqrt{5}x-(\\sqrt{5})^{2}) \\\\  & =3(x+3)({x}^{2}-5) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-5x+3{x}^{2}-15) \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}+9{x}^{2}-15x-45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as\n\n$$\n{-3,-\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{5}}={x\\in R\\,:\\,3{x}^{3}+9{x}^{2}-15x-45=0}.\n$$"}]}
